#20701
Atop a Cairn~
  You stand atop a cairn of rough granite.  From here you have a commanding
view of the entire island and lake.  The stones that make up this cairn are
rough and weathered.  You get the sense that they were moved here a very
long time ago, and with great difficulty.  There appears to be a narrow gap
in the stones which you might be able to squeeze down in to.  Otherwise,
you can climb down the cairn to the south.
~
207 0 4
D5
~
~
0 0 20702
S
#20702
Inside a Cairn~
  You are crouched in a small pocket inside a rock cairn.  The granite
walls are partially covered by thick, green moss here and there is a musty
dampness in the air.  A set of rough-hewn stairs leads down into darkness,
and a narrow gap in the cairn which you might be able to crawl through is
directly above your head.
~
